return array (
  'content' => '<p>Door handles are the most touched architectural metal on any project — entrance pulls, lever sets on bedrooms, flush plates on sliding panels. PVD-coated stainless handles deliver champagne, rose gold and black tones aligned with partitions and doors without solid-brass tarnish. Selecting finish, size and backset early prevents mismatches against doors fabricated elsewhere.</p><h2>PVD finishes on handles</h2><p>Champagne PVD suits warm neutral interiors common in Indian luxury apartments. Rose gold reads softer under warm LED downlights. Matte black gives graphic contrast on white doors and fluted glass.</p><p>Deep dive: <a href="/blog/pvd-finish-selection-guide-gold-rose-gold-champagne-black">PVD finish selection guide</a> and <a href="/blog/pvd-coating-explained">PVD coating explained</a>.</p><h2>Handle types by application</h2><p><strong>Pull handles</strong> — entrance and tall sliding doors; length affects ergonomics and proportion.</p><p><strong>Lever handles</strong> — hinged room doors; specify backset compatible with lock body.</p><p><strong>Flush pulls</strong> — sliding and pocket doors; recess depth must match door thickness.</p><p>Browse ranges on <a href="/shop/door-handles">door handles</a>.</p><h2>Sizing and ergonomics</h2><p>Entrance pulls often span 600–1200 mm on tall doors — see <a href="/blog/select-pull-handle-length-for-main-door">pull length guide</a>. Lever height typically 900–1050 mm AFF depending on door height and user profile.</p><p>Children and elderly users benefit from consistent lever height across the home — note on door schedule.</p><h2>Coordination with doors</h2><p>Order handles from same PVD batch as <a href="/studio/main-entrance-pvd-doors">entrance doors</a> and <a href="/studio/slim-profile-door-systems">slim profile doors</a> when possible. Mixed batches may show slight tone shift in daylight.</p><p>Specify fixing centres and rose diameter before door prep — misaligned bore holes are costly to fix in stainless doors.</p><h2>Care and replacement</h2><p>Wipe with soft cloth and pH-neutral cleaner; avoid abrasive pads. Individual handles can be replaced if damaged without remaking entire door — keep spare model reference on handover sheet.</p><h2>Ordering from Vyomika Atelier</h2><p>We supply PVD handles matched to our door and partition projects from our Delhi, India studio. International enquiries are reviewed project by project. Share door thickness, lock type and finish sample with enquiry.</p><h2>Backplate and rose options</h2><p>Round roses suit traditional interiors; square backplates align with contemporary door designs. Ensure rose diameter covers existing bore holes on retrofit doors.</p><p>Concealed fixings give cleaner appearance on entrance pulls but need access for maintenance — confirm screw approach before specifying.</p><h2>Commercial versus residential touch levels</h2><p>Hotel and office entrance pulls see higher daily cycles than villa doors. Satin and hairline finishes hide fine scratches better than mirror PVD on high-touch zones.</p><p>Anti-microbial expectations should be discussed with project consultants — PVD surfaces clean with standard protocols but are not a substitute for clinical specification where required.</p><h2>Lock and latch compatibility</h2><p>Mortise lock bodies from Indian brands vary in backset and faceplate width. Share lock model PDF with handle supplier before door prep.</p><p>Magnetic locks and electric strikes on automated entrances need pull handles mounted clear of actuator zones — note on door schedule early.</p><h2>Batch matching across the home</h2><p>Order entrance pulls, bedroom levers and wardrobe flush pulls in one PVD batch when colour consistency matters under daylight.</p><p>International enquiries are reviewed project by project — courier sample handles for approval before bulk production when site is outside India.</p><h2>Entrance sets versus interior sets</h2><p>Main entrance doors often combine a long vertical pull outside with a lever or thumbturn inside. Document both sides on the door schedule so bore prep aligns with lock body and pull backplate. Mixed suppliers for door leaf and handles cause the most common site conflicts.</p><h3>Sliding and pocket doors</h3><p>Flush pulls require recess depth matched to door thickness and track hardware. Pocket doors need pulls that do not catch on frame liners — specify rounded profiles or recessed finger pulls for narrow cavities.</p><h2>Finish durability on high-touch hardware</h2><p>PVD on stainless survives daily touch better than lacquered brass but mirror surfaces show fingerprints sooner than hairline. For family homes with children, prefer satin champagne or brushed rose gold on bedroom levers and reserve mirror gold for low-touch entrance accents.</p><p>Read <a href="/blog/pvd-coating-explained">PVD coating explained</a> for how vacuum deposition differs from thin-plate alternatives before comparing supplier quotes.</p><h2>Accessibility and family use</h2><p>Lever handles with comfortable return and pull handles with adequate diameter help users with reduced grip strength. Consistent lever height across the home — typically near 900–1050 mm above finished floor — reduces daily friction for mixed-age households.</p><p>Specify the same PVD batch on main entrance pulls and interior levers when visual continuity matters from lobby through living zones. See <a href="/blog/select-pull-handle-length-for-main-door">pull length guidance</a> for entrance proportion.</p><h2>Warranty and replacement planning</h2><p>Document handle model numbers and finish batch on handover sheets. Individual handles can be replaced after impact damage without remaking entire doors when records are clear. Keep one spare lever or pull on large hospitality projects where downtime matters.</p><p>Compare handle options on the <a href="/shop/door-handles">door handles shop page</a> and confirm bore centres with your door fabricator before placing combined orders.</p><h2>Security and smart-lock interfaces</h2><p>Smart locks and biometric readers may change backplate requirements on entrance doors. Confirm device dimensions with handle supplier so pulls and lock hardware do not overlap visually or functionally. Integrated solutions look cleaner when planned on one elevation drawing rather than assembled piecemeal on site.</p><p>Entrance sets ordered with doors from one fabricator reduce bore-centre mismatches that delay hotel and villa handovers.</p><h2>Ordering checklist</h2><p>Before release to production confirm door thickness, lock model, backset, pull length, PVD sample approval and delivery city. Missing any one item commonly delays bore prep or causes mismatch against adjacent <a href="/studio/main-entrance-pvd-doors">entrance doors</a> on the same project.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Select PVD door handles by finish sample under project lighting, correct length for entrance scale and lock compatibility for levers. Coordinate batch and bore centres with door fabricator before production — handles are small but visually decisive.</p><p>Shop <a href="/shop/door-handles">door handles</a>.</p><p>Match entrance scale in <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-luxury-main-entrance-door">luxury entrance guide</a>.</p><p>Compare finishes in <a href="/blog/pvd-finish-selection-guide-gold-rose-gold-champagne-black">finish selection guide</a>.</p><p>For a project-specific quotation, share floor plans or photos through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Architects and interior designers may also begin from the <a href="/professionals">professionals collaboration page</a>.</p>',
